    "body": "@annevk Fair enough - if browsers are indeed interested in broader options support as well, that would make plenty of sense (which would imply `ws` et al changing to support that instead, but that migration is also easy and non-breaking so not a huge problem).\n\nIt'd need some form of feature detection for browsers though, since `new WebSocket(url, { targetAddressSpace: 'private' })` throws in at least Chrome & FF today, so it wouldn't be safe for people to start using that API even if it existed. I'm not sure what the consensus is on approach for those kind of changes in browsers nowadays, but from my POV anyway (on the Node side) the end goal sounds fine.",
